<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! The edge frontier, 2026 ~ absence needs a signed boundary

A fifth fresh read of `K15` Wave B found that reading an empty edge board's absence as "aside" refused every healthy fleet's joins and key wraps, while reading it as "clear" lets a withheld raise pass. Claims read MEASURED (code or a cited source) or LEAD.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/findings`>>

!! Findings

# ''Nothing signed declares a board complete'' (both, MEASURED). Edge acts sign their own bytes (`edge-kapae.ts`); roll anchors commit past quorum heads; seat-roll receipts name known raises (`seat-duties.ts`); leases fold by maximum (`lease-frontier.ts`); `edgeStandingOf(undefined)` reads clear.
# ''The persona KEL cannot anchor raises today'' (both, MEASURED): its kinds cover rotation, veto and guardian enrolment, and its verifier rejects any other (`persona-kel.ts`). A separate certificate type, the KEL resolving its signer's key, needs no KEL change.
# ''Raise authority by board'' (Copilot, MEASURED): fleet edges raise by the holder (the fleet root) alone (`dyad.ts`); realm edges by quorum, vouch edges by holder and quorum (`realm-edges.ts`).
# ''A head proves inclusion, never absence, without an issuance rule'' (both; RFC 9162, KERI, Matrix device lists, UCAN revocation, did:plc). While a raise takes effect as a standalone signed act, no later head can prove a raise absent; a raise must enter the committed stream before it counts toward widening.
# ''Every useful analogue needs an issuer, a reader checkpoint and a comparison of views''; none supplies a global now. A stale valid head proves only its own boundary.
# ''Quorum arithmetic'' (Sol, LEAD): with n seats, threshold q and at most f Byzantine seats, conflicting quorums share an honest signer only where 2q − n > f; withheld signatures stall issuance.

<<~/ahu>>

